Tested-by: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz> # SMB2 (Pixel 3, Mi 8, OP 6 / 6T)
---
Changes in v5:
- Split charger-status decoding into smb2_map_charge_status() and
  smb5_map_charge_status() and call the match-data pointer.
  https://lore.kernel.org/all/44d4db6f-6b84-4cec-9e85-cb7b437bb7f9@ixit.cz/
- Drop smb_get_prop_health() and call data->get_prop_health() directly.
  https://lore.kernel.org/all/44d4db6f-6b84-4cec-9e85-cb7b437bb7f9@ixit.cz/
- Share one SMB2 parameter block between PMI8998 and PM660. The PM660
  match entry only sets the power-supply name.
  https://lore.kernel.org/all/44d4db6f-6b84-4cec-9e85-cb7b437bb7f9@ixit.cz/
- Use C99 for (int i = ...) in smb_init_hw().
  https://lore.kernel.org/all/44d4db6f-6b84-4cec-9e85-cb7b437bb7f9@ixit.cz/
- Rename the parameter pointer to chip->data and read chip->data->gen
  and the limits from it instead of copying them onto the chip.
  https://lore.kernel.org/all/b5f87468-20f1-437f-8610-518df679ee99@ixit.cz/
- Write CHARGING_ENABLE_CMD after CHGR_CFG2 selects software control,
  matching Fabricio Akio's for-next fix 1fba78714201 (not in this
  linux-next tag).
- Link to v4: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260820-submit-qcom-smbx-send-v1-v4-2-818dabb2771e@snyders.xyz

 drivers/power/supply/Kconfig     |   8 +-
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c | 775 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 2 files changed, 610 insertions(+), 173 deletions(-)

